1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,999
The mystery stock was Google, in September 2007.

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:09,590
It never closed below the buy price.

3
00:00:09,591 --> 00:00:13,181
Six weeks later it was up 32%.

4
00:00:13,182 --> 00:00:15,999
Buying was the easy half.

5
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:21,231
Then the market topped. Heavy-volume down days piled up.

6
00:00:21,232 --> 00:00:25,999
Google gave back its gains, week after week.

7
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:31,380
One simple sell rule: exit on a close below the 50-day average.

8
00:00:31,381 --> 00:00:34,501
That sold in December, up 20%.

9
00:00:34,502 --> 00:00:37,999
Holding and hoping: down 25% by March.

10
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:41,771
The buy was the easy half.

11
00:00:41,772 --> 00:00:45,999
Plan your sell before you need it.

12
00:00:48,200 --> 00:00:51,949
Lore 015. Next: Lore 016, Leaders travel in groups
